// Title: Suspicious Scan Loop Network
// Sigma ID: f8ad2e2c-40b6-4117-84d7-20b89896ab23
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: frack113
// Date: 2022-03-12 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: execution, T1059, discovery, T1018
// Description: Adversaries may attempt to get a listing of other systems by IP address, hostname, or other
//   logical identifier on a network that may be used for Lateral Movement from the current system
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate script
// References:
//   - https://github.com/redcanaryco/atomic-red-team/blob/f339e7da7d05f6057fdfcdd3742bfcf365fee2a9/atomics/T1018/T1018.md
//   - https://ss64.com/nt/for.html
//   - https://ss64.com/ps/foreach-object.html
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_susp_network_scan_loop.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (ProcessCommandLine contains "for " or ProcessCommandLine contains "foreach ") and (ProcessCommandLine contains "nslookup" or ProcessCommandLine contains "ping")
